id: DRAFT-tinydb-4.8.2-pypi-sdist-test-inventory
trigger_tool: python|pytest|pip
phase: testing|packaging
error_signature: collected 0 items|tests not found|source distribution.*tests
severity: 1
category: python, packaging, testing, portability
match_keywords: PyPI sdist, wheel, bundled tests, source archive, test inventory
title: A PyPI wheel can omit the upstream suite that is present in the same version's sdist
affected_scope: Pure-Python PyPI packages where release metadata includes tests in the sdist but excludes them from the wheel.
root_cause: PyPI wheel and source distribution are separate artifacts built with different inclusion rules; choosing the runtime wheel as the only test input can remove the upstream suite.
verification_cmd: python -c "import zipfile,tarfile; print('wheel tests', ...); print('sdist tests', ...)"; python -m pytest tests/ --collect-only -q
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: inspect-sdist-before-test-accounting
rec_description: Inventory the exact source archive and run its upstream tests before packaging runtime-only module files.
rec_command: sha256sum package.tar.gz; tar -tzf package.tar.gz | grep '/tests/'; python -m pytest tests/ -q
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual-archive-inventory
forbid_1_pattern: wheel.*(upstream tests|test count)|test.*wheel.*zero|pytest.*0 items
forbid_1_reason: The wheel is a runtime artifact and can exclude test files that the sdist intentionally ships.
forbid_1_consequence: The recipe may undercount the upstream suite or declare no tests even though the pinned source release provides them.
principles: R51
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [DRAFT-pyjson5-0.15.0-pure-python-no-build-packaging, DRAFT-VENDP-PUREPY-DEP-CLOSURE]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
